    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0260" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11059: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-05T16:00:00+08:00">August 5, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 5—10:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>668. Legation’s 663, August 4, 11 a.m. The following from American Consul at
                    Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 4, 5 p.m. Substance of Adams’ August 3, 10 a.m. to
                                Washington:<anchor n="74" xml:id="d173-f1"/> Advised [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Advice?</hi>] to withdraw telegraphed to O’Shea,
                            who is requested to notify other Americans in Kanchow.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d173-f1" n="74" xml:id="d173-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 663, August 4, 11 a.m., from the Minister in China, <ref
                        target="#pg161">p. 161</ref>.</p>
